eing grateful. [3940] The paper he is looking for is quickly found. [3941] The door opened, and someone entered the room. [3942] Hosaka read the English paper, a work written before his birth. The author was probably no longer alive. Would his own papers someday be read in some distant future world... How long would this chain of information continue? The content seemed interesting, but there were many unfamiliar terms. Just reading the abstract yielded several unknown words. [3943] Feeling someone approach, Hosaka lifted his gaze from the book. [3944] \"Hello,\" a woman said with a smile. [3945] Hosaka nearly dropped the thick book in his hand. [3946] \"Dr. Makoto Edogawa...\"\n[3947] Edogawa's body stiffened like steel. [3948] Her hair had changed. She had short, wavy hair that was a reddish-brown color. She wore glasses with pale pink lenses that were too large for her. A small plaid shirt and a long skirt with pleats. She wore small shoes. She looked like the most ordinary girl in a university. [3949] However, the person standing there, Edogawa would not mistake, was Miyuki Futaki, no, Miyuki Shiki. [3950] She leaned against the wall, smiling with her white teeth. \"I hope you're doing well, Edogawa-sensei.\" [3951] Her hands were behind her back, her chin tucked in, staring intently at Shimizu. [3952] \"Why\u2026\" Shimizu finally managed to speak, his hands gripping the open paper. Without that, they seemed to tremble uncontrollably. [3953] \"We agreed to meet again, didn't we?\" Akita Shiki said with interest. \"Your lab's security system is too weak. I read the emails between you and Ms. Nishiyama.\" [3954] \"The police are after you.\" [3955] \"Don't say such obvious things,\" Shiki said indifferently. \"Let's go to another room. This place\u2026 it's too musty. I'm about to sneeze.\" [3956] \"Okay, let's go downstairs\u2026\" Naito hurriedly put the book back on the shelf. [3957] \"Is it okay? You came here to look for something, right?\" [3958] \"Yes, it's fine. I can come back anytime.\" The two of them walked out of the room in silence. [3959] As they stepped into the hallway, she suddenly stopped and looked up. [3960] \"Let's go upstairs\u2026\" Shiono said. [3961] \"This is the meeting room up here.\" [3962] \"Can we go to the rooftop?\" [3963] \"Are you planning to commit suicide?\" Shusui said, \"We can't go to the rooftop.\" [3964] Shinobu Shichen chuckled softly. [3965] \"I wouldn't commit suicide. If I wanted to, I would have done it already\u2026 It's on a hill, I just want to see the scenery\u2026\"\n[3966] They descended the stairs. Makoto Shishou followed behind Shishou. Halfway down, Shishou turned to look at her, noticing her hands behind her back as she slowly descended one step at a time. She must not be used to walking down stairs. [3967] \"Did you also make a card?\" Shishou asked, \"You can't enter without logging in.\" [3968] \"Yes, I logged in. It's my real name, Makoto Shishou.\" Shishou replied, \"There are sixteen books of mine here, eighty-four papers. I just checked. Most of them are there...\"\n[3969] \"There are two of my books...\" Shishou said, \"But it's more than Isaac Newton. He only has one.\" [3970] Makoto Shishou smiled at Shishou's humor. [3971] Through the brown tinted glass, the entire campus could be seen from the hall. It was bright outside due to the intense heat, resembling boiling foam. There were no pedestrians in sight. [3972] Fuyuyuki felt that she walked awkwardly. [3973] They sat side by side on comfortable single sofas. Fuyuyuki's face was right in front of Nishikawa. He shuddered at the incredible closeness. He felt that she was close yet seemed unattainable. He thought that, although she was right in front of him, she was like a distant, unreachable deity. [3974] Nishikawa, taking a moment to calm himself, thought that Fuyuyuki, no, this person, was a deity in disguise. A puppet controlled by a deity. [3975] Yes, a puppet. [3976] Dr. Makoto Hasegawa looks at Kyota