o killed three people. No, all of this was her doing. Detective-san, you should contact your department right away. It's already too late\u2026\"\n[3806] The Shimizu nodded, wide-eyed. [3807] \"Genius... a genius,\" said Sugawara, nodding repeatedly. \"She won't be swayed by our ideas... she's been ahead from the start...\"\n[3808] \"But Future-san only speaks English, doesn't she?\" asked the head of the West Garden. [3809] \"She's a genius...\" Sugawara smiled. Then, he blew smoke rings with the cigarette in his hand. [3810] \"She's Dr. Akira Miyuki.\" [3811] 8\n[3812] Zuo Chi and Shiyuzhuang said \"We'll be right back\" and left the room. After that, no one in the chief's office spoke. [3813] Xucun remembered it was summer. [3814] The university was on summer vacation. Of course, even though it was summer vacation, it only meant there were no classes. Generally, scholars like Xucun, who are research-oriented, don't even realize it's summer vacation, let alone Obon. Xucun's research lab had windows, but it was basically the same as the True Ardor Research Institute. [3815] He smoked, thinking about what he would think about when he returned to the university. The murder case had ended. At least, Xucun's interest in this case had quickly disappeared. [3816] Detective Shimizu picked up the helicopter model on the chief's desk. [3817] \"The helicopter was invented by Leonardo da Vinci,\" Detective Shimizu said to himself, \"before the airplane. It's strange that it took humans so long to realize the principles of flight... At one point, they thought that birds flapping their wings pushed air downward... That was the reason for the failure...\"\n[3818] No one paid attention to Detective Shimizu's words, except for Yoshiko, who chuckled quietly in the corner. Miyuki seemed a little worried and approached Detective Shimizu. [3819] \"Teacher...\" Miyuki said, \"You said that Dr. Shinjiro Ardor was the murderer...\"\n[3820] \"Yes,\" Detective Shimizu put the helicopter model back on the table and exhaled smoke from one hand. \"I'm not an expert in this field, so I don't know the specifics of multiple personalities... No, I mean, what's physically going on. But, originally, there are multiple personalities within one individual, right? Some people might not believe it, but at least for me... I have many different personalities. I personally believe that very few people have a single personality...\"\n[3821] There was still no reaction from everyone to Xiangchuan's words. [3822] Xiangchuan turned around and spoke to everyone. [3823] \"I mentioned that Japan is a liquid society and the West is a solid society, and this can also be applied to individuals... The Japanese, their multiple personalities within their bodies are like liquids mixed together and stirred. The West's thoughts are not like that. They are still solid. Will Japan gradually become solid in the future?\" [3824] Yes, Shigemori had said that solid things become liquid when looked at for a long time. Xiangchuan remembered. [3825] \"Teacher, what are you talking about?\" Doctor Gakushou stroked his beard. [3826] \"Nothing, just daydreaming,\" Sekigawa said, extinguishing his cigarette. \"What are you all doing?\" [3827] The head of the West office, Nishiyama, opened the door and stepped out, followed by a crestfallen Tsuzuki. [3828] \"Can you explain it to us, teacher?\" Tsuzuki approached Sekigawa. [3829] \"Explain what?\" Sekigawa asked. [3830] \"What you said\u2026\" Tsuzuki exaggeratedly said, \"We've taken emergency measures in Aichi and Mie prefectures to capture Aragaki Futaba\u2026 But I don't understand. Can you explain it to us?\" [3831] \"Yes, I don't understand what you mean either.\" Bowayong said. [3832] Shuzhuo lit a cigarette. \"Everything is clear.\" [3833] \"Teacher...,\" Menghui walked over and whispered softly, \"We need not just the answer, but also your explanation...\"\n[3834] \"Ah, so that's it...,\" Shuzhuo nodded, \"Does everyone need it?\" [3835] Everyone in the room nodded. Shuzhuo was surprised. [3836] \"Alright then\u2026\" X\u012bchu\u01cen puffed out smoke rings as he slowly walked towards the center of the room. \"Where should I start? Ah, let's start by explaining why Red Magic went out of control first\u2026\"\n[3837] \"I already understand that,\" said Mizukami. \"Red Magic is a Trojan horse itself\u2026\"\n[3838] \"I have a question about this,\" said M\u00e9ngr\u00ec, raising her hand like a student. No, she was a true student. \"At that time, Dr. Akagi said that everything became 'F' that day, right? The calendar of the lady computer also had this. So, what is 'F'?\" [3839] \"F is fifteen,\" X\u012bchu\u01cen answered immediately. [3840] \"Fifteen? Is it fifteen?\" M\u00e9ngr\u00ec furrowed her eyebrows. \"Is it the 'F' of fifteen? But\u2026if so, there are many 'F's in fourteen (fourteen), five (five), and four (four).\" [3841] \"It's hexadecimal, Oshimura.\" Fujisawa answered. \"In the Red Magic program, the variable used to calculate time is integer, which means it's an integer type. Computers process numbers in binary, but the program groups four digits together and represents them in hexadecimal. That's one bit. In general integer types, it's two bytes\u2026 because there are four bits, so in hexadecimal, we can use four digits, which means we can use all numbers up to 16 raised to the power of four.\" [3842] \"16 raised to the power of four?\" Yuria questioned. \"That's 65536\u2026 Is that the 256 times 256 calculation you mentioned?\" [3843] \"That's right, that's the resolution, the threshold. I can still remember 16 squared\u2026 In the program, the integer-type variable, if it's an unsigned integer, starts from 0 and goes up to positive integers. Double-precision integers can go up to 8 bits, while single-precision short integers can only go up to 4 bits. Starting from 0, that means the largest number is 65535, which is one less than 65536.\" [3844] \"What does that have to do with F?\" Yuria asked. [3845] \"In hexadecimal, the number on the ones place goes up to 15\u2026\" Fujisawa said. \"But we only have the numbers 0 to 9 in the decimal system. In the decimal system, 10 is a two-digit number. 10 is represented by 1 and 0. In hexadecimal, 16 starts to become a two-digit number 10 (one zero). If we only use the numbers 0 to 9, hexadecimal cannot be used. So\u2026 in general, the numbers 10 to 15 are represented by the letters A, B, C, D, E, F. F is the 15 in the decimal system. Just like the 9 in the decimal system, F is the largest single digit in hexadecimal.\" [3846] \"So everything becomes 15...?\" M\u00e8nghu\u00ec seemed to be confused again. [3847] \"In the 1 to 10, 7 is alone...\" Xiyuan remembered Ms. Truehata's words and said, \"From 1 to 16... B and D become alone...\"\n[3848] \"B is 11, D is 13.\" M\u00e8nghu\u00ec answered, \"Ah, that's right... If it's within 16, 7 is no longer alone. Because there's 14... Dr. Truehata was talking about that... But what if everything becomes F?\" [3849] \"The maximum value of a single-precision integer type in the decimal system, 65535, is represented as FFFF in hexadecimal, which is the largest four-digit number. Counting from 0000, we can count up to all the digits becoming F... Counting until all the digits become F is the timer. This is the limit device. Dr. Truehata planned this at least seven years ago. From Dr. Truehata's room, there is no way to tamper with the system. But Dr. Truehata participated in the development of that system. The limit device is set to 65535 hours after the start, which is 65535 hours later. Dr. Truehata's sand timer started before 65535 hours that day.\" [3850] Xiyuan continued to look at everyone. \"The rest is the same as what Xiyuan said on the cloud. The anomaly in Red Magic was not caused by human intervention, but was set up in the program. That day, the yellow door couldn't be opened. Then, at the predetermined time, the door automatically opened. Because it was a performance, the lighting was dimmed and brightened. Everything was set up. However, for Deborah, who was developed after that, everything was an unforeseen error. Please check the source code of Red Magic carefully. The evidence is still there.\" [3851] 9\n[3852] \"Okay, let's move on to Dr. Momota's puzzle in the room...\" Fujisawa unconsciously walks around the room. This is a habit of his when teaching. \"However, Mr. Nishiyama has basically revealed the truth. In Dr. Momota's room, there was someone else besides Dr. Momota. And from the environmental conditions, we conclude that the person is Dr. Momota's child.\" [3853] \"Wait, wait...,\" Shibazaki raises his hand, \"But it was said that it's impossible...\"\n[3854] \"Wait, I don't accept it,\" Fujisawa says as he walks and looks down, \"When I accept a question, I always say this...\"\n[3855] Shibazaki looks at the department head, Nishiyama, with a bitter smile, but the department head's expression remains unchanged. [3856] \"There is a robot named MICHIRU in the inner bedroom...\u201d Nishida continued, \"It can unlock and lock. This has been confirmed. But why create this robot?\u201d\n[3857] \"It was a playmate for the child...\u201d Momiji immediately said. [3858] \"I acknowledge your statement...\u201d Nishida smiled, \"But that's secondary. I believe the initial motive was not this. It is likely that someone locked the bedroom door from the inside. Then they fell asleep. Therefore, Dr. Shinagawa could not sleep in bed all night. Imagine such a situation. For this, Dr. Shinagawa created the robot. Because it can unlock and lock...\u201d\n[3859] \"Boring, just take the lock off... why make a robot?\u201d Dr. Koyama smiled. [3860] \"That's the kind of thinking that only a genius can understand.\u201d Nishida shrugged, \"The child rebelled against his mother, locked the door, but fell asleep right away. Dr. Shinagawa did not remove the lock. She allowed the child to lock the door. However, after the child fell asleep, she let the robot unlock the door... I think it's a natural behavior...\"\n[3861] \"Regardless, after seeing that robot, I believe there is another person. And that person is a child\u2026 a girl who was locked inside fifteen years ago. No one has gone in since then. No, even if they did, they would come out immediately. Luggage has also undergone strict inspection. There are no channels\u2026 However, since the body was decomposed in the end, there must have been two people\u2026 How about it? From such environmental conditions, do you think there are any other possible answers? Can you come up with any other conclusions?\" [3862] \"Dr. Makoto was locked in that room when she was already pregnant with another child. Seven years later, a time-limited device called Red Magic was set up. Dr. Makoto calculated everything and decided to implement her plan.\" [3863] \"The same plan as what the Saotome said\u2026\" Shimizu looked at Momiji and said kindly, \"I always believed her plan was to have her daughter kill her. However, it wasn't like that\u2026\"\n[3864] \"Not?\" He just finished speaking, and Momiji immediately widened her eyes and put her hands over her mouth, retreating, \"Ah\u2026 what's going on\u2026\"\n[3865] \"Yes\u2026 it didn't go according to Dr. Makoto's imagination. Because\u2026\" He was at a loss for words, \"because\u2026 Dr. Makoto's child couldn't kill her mother. She couldn't follow her mother's orders. Because her child\u2026 is not a genius\u2026\"\n[3866] \"Not...?\" Moe's eyes reddened. [3867] \"It was not Dr. Makoto's daughter who killed her mother... It was Dr. Makoto who killed her daughter. Dr. Makoto's child was just an ordinary child. She was not a genius. She could not kill her own mother. She could not understand her mother's thoughts... As the deadline approached, this judgment was very cruel for Dr. Makoto. She must have been very troubled by this calculation error. That's why she left three pieces of information and also left a schedule on the calendar. And in the virtual space just now, she also said those confessions. I believe that all of this... was based on her guilt after killing her child. Everything did not proceed according to her wishes. This was an incomplete result.\" [3868] \"Not having a name always makes one feel pitiful, so let's call the victim Dai-rii-san. Dr. Makoto dressed her daughter in a wedding dress... The body we saw was Dai-rii-san. If we assume this hypothesis, everything becomes simple and makes sense. For example... The reason for cutting off the hands and feet from the body is very simple... To hide Dr. Makoto's fingerprints... That is, only two hands need to be cut off. Because Dr. Makoto was a suspect in the incident fifteen years ago, the police station must have kept her fingerprint records. Moreover, cutting off the feet may have been to make it easier to put Dai-rii-san on P1, but on the other hand, it would be easier to conceal this action in relation to fingerprints. At first, we reasoned that the killer wanted to use Dr. Makoto's right hand to open the door. This was probably also within Dr. Makoto's calculations. However, if Dr. Makoto was the killer, she could have opened the door with her right hand... \"\n[3869] \"When did the change to the plan begin? Not being killed by someone else, but killing one's own child... I continue. Of course, everything is just a guess... I think it was probably three years ago. Probably when the wedding dress was purchased. Why? Because from that time on, Dai-rii-san replaced Dr. Makoto in the TV footage. However... I think it must have taken a lot of time to wipe off Dai-rii-san's fingerprints in the room. From then on, Dai-rii-san was put on gloves... This was a preparation to not leave Dai-rii-san's fingerprints. \" [3870] \"Dai-rii-san developed earlier than Dr. Makoto... However, even if mother and daughter looked alike, it was not possible for Dai-rii-san to suddenly replace Dr. Makoto. However, Dr. Makoto acted as a multiple personality. At the same time, she kept the impression of Dai-rii-san being fourteen years old outside. Dr. Makoto is twenty-nine years old this year, and she has grown up and grown taller in the fifteen years, and her weight should have increased. However, people outside could only know her situation through the display. Various conditions made their alternation possible... \"\n[3871] \"I heard that Dr. Makoto had lost weight three years ago. But did he really lose weight? I think it was when Doi-chan took over. Doi-chan spoke in the same tone as her mother. With her long hair and headphones, no one would know. I think Doi-chan was told what to say by Dr. Makoto when she spoke about work in front of the camera. She spoke in front of the camera in the same way as her mother... She might occasionally speak in her own language, which is what they call the Doi personality inside Dr. Makoto's body\u2026\"\n[3872] \"What I see is Miss D\u00e0o Li\u00fa,\" M\u00e9ng Hu\u00ec whispered, \"Yes, she is wearing gloves\u2026\"\n[3873] \"Dr. Akikusa is no longer the young girl you all imagine her to be,\" continued Saito. \"She has used the impression of her as a fourteen-year-old girl to complete this transition. These past three years, the one you have seen before you is Miss. Oozora.\" [3874] \"Continuing the previous topic... Dr. Akutagawa murdered Dojima Miss and dismembered her body. He then cleaned the bathroom and prepared for his escape that day. Dr. Akutagawa had P1 carry Dojima Miss's body out, taking advantage of the commotion outside to leave the room. This also matches what the West Garden said. By using the computer clock's automatic return to one minute, he saved the file with the same name, resulting in missing one minute of the recording data. The clock's change was also pre-set through Red Magic's hourglass.\n <Assistant> I have read the book and I will answer the question you ask.\n\nPassage 4:\nDialogue between User and 