uct is a multiple of 7, while the other group doesn't have a 7, so they can't be equal.\" [62] \"You see, only 7 is alone,\" Trueharada says. \"The personality in me with a motive to kill my parents is only Trueharada Yuki. So, if my body killed my parents, I wouldn't forget. Only I am 7... B and D are too.\" [63] (B and D...) Momiji doesn't understand what she means. [64] \"What's your motive?\" Momiji asks. [65] \"I don't know... maybe to go out and play...?\" Trueharada answers from the screen. \"There's evidence to suggest that. Have you thought about the real meaning of motives? Is that why you're here?\" [66] \"No.\" [67] \"Then let's get to the point,\" Ms. Makino said, for the first time taking her eyes off Bunru. \"You have 17 minutes and 40 seconds left.\" [68] 2\n[69] Bunru remembered that it was summer. [70] Carefully observing the girl in the video (yes, it was appropriate to call her that), she noticed she was wearing a white sweater and could occasionally see thin gloves on her hands. She was probably in the middle of doing something. No, this place was originally devoid of seasons, like a sealed plastic container. [71] \"You've been in this room for fifteen years, haven't you?\" Hanae recalled her prepared questions, \"What changes have you experienced being in a place without seasons or day and night for fifteen years? What changes did you experience after losing your parents?\" [72] \"First of all, I refuse to answer that question. I was never here because of free will, so my thoughts can't possibly change positively in this special environment. However, some things naturally arose within me, which in a way helped me settle down and recognize reality.\" [73] \"I don't know. I... lost consciousness after my parents died. I thought everything was meaningless and lost interest in human society. Your opinion will become an assumption and sample data for me to survive and create my model.\" [74] \"Your words are quite interesting.\" [75] \"What you call